[Music]  despite having very few first-party  exclusives in 2022 Xbox still had a  pretty strong year thanks to some  excellent additions to Xbox game pass  which grew its catalog with dozens of  fantastic games here are the five best  Xbox games of 2022 as selected by  Gamespot as well as five honorable  mentions that you need to check out ASAP  2022 was truly the year of vampire  survivors the Smash Hit bullet hell  Survival game that took Steam and Xbox  by storm while it might not look like a  shiny Triple A release when it comes to  satisfying gameplay Loops that'll keep  you hooked for hours it is unmatched but  what do you do in Vampire survivors you  survive for 30 minutes that's the goal  the moment-to-moment gameplay is  relatively simple all you have to do is  move your character who will then  automatically attack enemies that will  begin to swarm you enemies drop gems  which you then pick up to gain  experience and level up unlocking new  weapons and Buffs it is so simple to  play and the more you do the more the  game gets its hooks in you from fusing  weapons to get more powerful evolved  versions to unlocking every stage and  character to even defeating the Grim  Reaper himself there is so much to do  and it's bite-sized 30 minute stages are  perfect to dip into  pentiment is an adventure game set in  the 16th century you play as Andreas  Marla an artist working for an Abbey in  Bavaria who was also aiming to finish  his Masterpiece on the side a murder at  the Abbey is the spark that lights the  Powder Keg that is the relationship  between the Abbey the townsfolk and The  Peasants and somehow it's up to Andreas  to investigate the conspiracy at the  heart of it all Andreas is a Stranger in  a Strange Land just as we the players  are to a rapidly changing 16th century  Bavarian Society pentiment follows the  role each person as well as the church  plays and to prevent it from being  overwhelming offers an in-depth glossary  and character guide to help out in a  pinch much has been made about  pentiman's art style which is a love  letter to the art of the time but it's  the game's characters that really shine  especially as we see them grow and  change over time if you long to dig into  an intriguing mystery maybe learn some  things too then pentiment is the game  for you  three movies one incredible story when  an actress goes missing it's up to you  to scrub through her three unreleased  movies and behind the scenes footage to  find Clues and try and discover the  truth of what happened to her things  might seem straightforward at first  glance but the deeper you dig the more  secrets you'll uncover immortality  utilizes FMV to tell its story and  features some of the best performances  you'll see all year particularly from  man and Gage who plays the lead role of  Marissa Marcel in his 8 out of 10 review  Mark Delaney wrote despite and sometimes  because of the dizzying effect of  falling down the rabbit hole immortality  becomes another standout narrative it's  similar to its predecessors telling lies  and her story in some key ways but more  thought-provoking too and certainly more  unnerving than you'll be prepared for  grounded is a survival crafting game  with a Twist you're a kid who's been  shrunken down to the size of an ant and  it's up to you and some Pals to survive  in the backyard gather resources build a  base and fend off the creepy crawlies  that are out to get you but everything  is coated with a childlike sense of  adventure making it feel more like Honey  I Shrunk the Kids or the borrowers  grounded has been in the Xbox Early  Access program for a couple of years but  hit 1.0 in 2022 in his 8 out of 10  review Mark Delaney said the Fantastical  setup makes for an immediately  intriguing setup and to further stylize  it as a uniquely childlike Adventure  polish it Beyond most of its peers and  set it in a world full of familiar  sights to see in startling new ways  makes grounded no small feat  as dusk Falls is an interactive  narrative game that follows the Fallout  of a robbery gone wrong and how the  event impacts the lives of two families  in small town Arizona your decisions  have consequences and the outcomes for  the characters vary wildly depending on  the choices that you make if that sounds  like too much pressure get some friends  involved to help out as you can play the  game with up to eight friends both  online and locally in his 9 out of 10  review Mark Delaney wrote by way of  incredible voice acting a compelling and  expertly written script and a bounty of  pause-worthy choices along the game's  elaborate branching paths it establishes  itself as an instant classic in the  narrative Adventure genre those were  gamespot's 5 best Xbox games of 2022 but  since you've been good this year here  are five more if you're a fan of Pikmin  you'll feel right at home with tinykin  as Milo an astronaut who has crash  landed in a house it's up to you to  gather Little Critters called tinykin to  help you get home a tinykin by itself  can't do much but when you gather a  small group together you can alter them  to lift heavy items break items that are  in your way and even make currents to  power on electronics tinykin is a  delightful puzzle platformer where  ordinary items have multiple uses and  there's a secret tucked behind every  corner each of tinykins levels is set in  a different room of a 90s era Family  Home and with your tiny kin you're  tasked with various objectives from the  bugs who call the house home getting  around the large spaces is a breeze not  only can you Glide using your bubble  pack but you can also speed around on a  bar of soap which is just as fun and  satisfying as it sounds in her 8 out of  10 review Jess Howard said tinykin is a  delightful callback to 90s  collect-a-thons and Platformers with  just the right amount of new ideas and  iterations  okay okay I know Elden ring is not an  XBox exclusive by any means because it  also came out on PC and Playstation but  it did win our game of the year award  and it's a game you should be playing  regardless of which platform you own  sorry switch owners because Elden ring  is from software's magnum opus and will  go down in history as one of the best  open world if not one of the best games  of all time as a lowly tarnished you  awaken in the lands between an enormous  world full of mystery Discovery and  danger and must fight your way to become  the Elden Lord in typical from software  the journey is punishing but Elden ring  takes a lot of strides in becoming the  most approachable from soft game yet if  an encounter is too difficult for you  there is a whole world to explore full  of hundreds of weapons and spells to  create a build that works for you in his  10 out of 10 review Timor Hussein wrote  from software's latest is a masterpiece  of open world design that places  exploration and player agency at the  heart of the experience that delicate  orchestration of highs and lows and the  build up and release of tension that  from software has mastered coupled with  the thrill of freeform exploration and  Discovery is an intoxicating cocktail of  game design  Beacon Pines is a game with an  incredibly intriguing premise the game  is set within a book and you play the  role of both the book's main character  and its reader along the adventure you  collect golden charms which can then be  used to replace specific words in the  story which then changes how things play  out Beacon Pines is a unique take on the  choice driven narrative genre and  manages to balance being cute and creepy  all at the same time so what more could  you want  and nobody saves the world you're a  nobody and that's okay when an ancient  threat called the Calamity awakens it's  up to you to stop it by transforming  into a creature that's up to the task  whether that's a ghost horse dragon or  even a slug Yes you heard that right you  can swap forms to use abilities suitable  for the situation you're in as you  complete quests you level up each form  and unlock new ones providing a  compelling gameplay Loop where the next  unlock is always around the corner mix  that with the procedurally generated  Dungeons and nobody Saves the World As a  Dungeon Crawler that offers so much  variety that it's tough to put it down  in his 9 out of 10 review Steve Watts  was enamored with the game saying after  finishing nobody Saves the World I went  right back to it there were still  dungeons to explore powers to unlock  secrets to uncover and a new game plus  mode to conquer when a game is this much  frictionless fun it's hard to resist a  plague tale Requiem is the sequel to  2019's a plague tale innocence and once  again follows amicia and her little  brother Hugo as they desperately search  cure for Hugo's disease the game is set  in France where a deadly plague is being  carried by rats and it's not just the  bite that you need to avoid soldiers of  the Inquisition are constantly on your  tail hoping to use Hugo's condition for  their own gains a plague tale Requiem is  a finely crafted puzzle action adventure  game with a deeply affecting story about  siblings at its heart it's not truly an  XBox exclusive but it did launch as a  day one game pass title earlier this  year  those were our picks for the best Xbox  games of 2022 if you want to know the  best PlayStation switch and PC games of  the year make sure to subscribe to  Gamespot on YouTube or check out  gamespot.com we also have an in-depth  video on our game of the year Elden ring  and just why it got that coveted title  you can find me on Twitter at Lucy James  games and I'll see you next time  thank you  [Music]

